 "text": "Reference\nAAR 2023\nAudit Observations\nAudit Recommendations\nWe recommended and Management agreed\nto:\n6. The City was unable to identify and\nObservation No. 6 appropriate various PPAs for LCCAP in CY 2023,\nPage 95\nwhich is not Inconsonance with Section 14 of\nRepublic Act (RA) No. 9729, otherwise known as, 6.11.1. Promptly create the City's ICCAP Core\nthe Climate Change Act of 2009, as amended\nTeam in accordance with Pparagraph. 3.1.1\nof DILG-MC No. 2014-135 and Section. 7 of\nthe City's LCCAP to facilitate the proper\nplanning, prioritization, funding,\nImplementation and monitoring/assessment\nof proposed climate change PPAs; and\n6.11.2. Ensure that approved climate change\nPPAs are aligned with the City's LCCAP and\nfunded from the City's IRA (now NTA) In\naccordance with Section. 14 of RA No. 9729.\nAGENCY ACTION PLAN\nPerson/Dept.\nTarget Implementation Date\nAction Plan\nStatus of\nImplementation\nResponsible\nFrom\nTo\nOffice of the City\nMayor\nOngoing\nOffice of the City\nMayor\nOngoing\nCY 2022 AAR,\n7. The City has not remitted P393.564 million\nObservation No. 6, representing the amounts withheld as of\nPage 81\nDecember 31, 2022 for the accounts of the BIR,\nGSIS, Pag-IBIG and PhilHealth, contrary to the\nappertaining legal prescriptions.\nWe relterated our recommendation that\nManagement direct the OCAT and CTO to\nremit the P393.564 million to the BIR, GSIS,\nPag-IBIG and PhilHealth without further\ndelay.\nOCAT and CТО\nOngoing\nCY 2021 AAR,\n8. Seven hundred twenty-three (723) cases of\nObservatlon No. 4, double payment of emergency subsidy/financial\nPage 83\nassistance (FA) to beneficiarles In COVID-19\nlockdown translated to a total payment of\nP8.424 million In excess of the amounts legally\nauthorized,\nWe recommended that Management:\na. Establish the accountability for and recover\nthe excess payment of emergency subsidy\nand FA; and\nb. In coordination with the DSWD, supply the\nmissing beneficiary information necessary In\nthe full validation of the payments of the\nsubject emergency subsidy/FA.\nOffice of the Mayor/\nManila Department\nof Social Welfare/\nCity Legal Office\nOffice of the Mayor/\nManila Department\nof Social Welfare\nOngoing\nOngoing\nReason for Partial/Delay/\nNon-Implementation, if\napplicable\nThe management Is\ncurrently in the process of\ncreating the Core Team.\nThe necessary documents\nwill be submitted to COA\nonce finalized and\napproved.\nAction Taken/Action to\nbe Taken\nThe OCAT In\ncoordination with CTO\nIs continuously\nremitting the remaining\nunremitted amount to\nIssues related to\nemployees detalls and\nInformation (for Clarif\nItems) for GSIS. On the\nother hand the amount\npayable to BIR reflects the date.\nwithholding taxes related\nto unpald payable to\ndifferent suppliers.\n",
